%\todo{EAJ: i commented the first part as it is already in intro? Maybe later paragraph needs to be adapted accordinlgy.}% In a recent paper \cite*{bourgey2024smile}, the authors attempted to calibrate various stochastic volatility models (rough Bergomi, rough Heston, two-factor Bergomi, and Heston) to the term structure of SPX ATM implied volatility, skew and SSR. They observed that the calibrated SSR of these models ``significantly deviate from the empirical market behavior around the calibration date", suggesting some degree of inconsistency between this family of models to the empirical dynamic properties of the SPX volatility surface. 

