ensures that all DC demands  are met with probability at least $1-\alpha.$ Figure \ref{fig:asymp_char} illustrates the optimal cost $v_\alpha^\ast$ for different demand distributions, along with  (i)  the respective best-fitting functions with growth rate $s_\alpha^r = (\bar{F}^{-1}(\alpha))^r$ and (ii) the  asymptotic characterization $v^\ast s_\alpha^r$ identified in  Theorem \ref{thm:solution_convergence}.


